# =============================================================================
# Bridges extracted from FoodOn's own definition text   (10)
# =============================================================================
# FoodOn frequently states an origin in prose while asserting nothing.
# Paprika's definition reads 'derived from the dried fruit of several
# varieties of Capsicum annuum L.'; pasta's reads 'an unleavened dough of
# wheat flour'. Each of these was extracted, passed five guards, and signed
# off against that one class's own sentence. Prose is not an axiom, so a
# human ruling is recorded per class.


### acorn flour  --RO:0001000-->  oak tree
#   rule:       E: definition mining
#   evidence:   A flour that is made by grinding acorns, the nuts of oak trees, after they have been properly processed to remove tannin.
#   confidence: high
#   reviewer:   Matt
#   Extracted from FoodOn's own definition text and signed off per class.
#   Definition names the source outright and unambiguously: 'a flour made by
#   grinding acorns, the nuts of oak trees, after they have been properly
#   processed to remove tannin'. Leaf class, no existing out-edges, one
#   source. `oak tree` is parented `temperate-zone nut producing plant`, so
#   acorn flour also becomes reachable from a tree-nut query -- correct, an
#   acorn is a nut.
obo:FOODON_00005523 rdfs:subClassOf [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
    owl:someValuesFrom obo:FOODON_03411715 ] .
local:patch-793d7522213d a local:Patch ;
    local:patchSection "mined" ;
    local:patchTarget obo:FOODON_00005523 ;
    local:patchProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
    local:patchValue obo:FOODON_03411715 ;
    local:patchRule "E: definition mining" ;
    local:patchEvidence "A flour that is made by grinding acorns, the nuts of oak trees, after they have been properly processed to remove tannin." ;
    local:patchConfidence "high" ;
    rdfs:comment "Extracted from FoodOn's own definition text and signed off per class. Definition names the source outright and unambiguously: 'a flour made by grinding acorns, the nuts of oak trees, after they have been properly processed to remove tannin'. Leaf class, no existing out-edges, one source. `oak tree` is parented `temperate-zone nut producing plant`, so acorn flour also becomes reachable from a tree-nut query -- correct, an acorn is a nut." ;
    dcterms:creator "Matt" ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-10"^^xsd:date .

### croziflette  --RO:0001000-->  buckwheat plant
#   rule:       E: definition mining
#   evidence:   A tartiflette except that small squares of pasta, crozets de Savoie (usually made from buckwheat but sometimes durum) are used instead of potatoes.
#   confidence: medium
#   reviewer:   Matt
#   Extracted from FoodOn's own definition text and signed off per class.
#   MEDIUM, not high, and the reason is in the definition: 'crozets de Savoie
#   (usually made from buckwheat BUT SOMETIMES DURUM)'. That is a recipe
#   choice, the same shape as the may_contain overrides that are deliberately
#   kept out of the closure. Signed anyway under the recall-first policy,
#   because the distinction that matters is which way an error falls:
#   buckwheat allergy is anaphylactic and crozets are USUALLY buckwheat, so a
#   buckwheat-avoider must see this dish. The cost is over-inclusion for the
#   durum variant, which is the safe direction. TWO GAPS THIS DOES NOT CLOSE,
#   recorded so nobody reads the dish as mapped: (1) croziflette is a
#   multi-component dish (tartiflette base) and so also contains milk via
#   reblochon, pork via bacon and allium via onion -- FoodOn asserts none of
#   those and this bridge adds none of them; (2) the durum variant means it
#   may contain gluten, and since buckwheat is gluten-free it will NOT appear
#   on a gluten query. Revisit if a dish-level ingredient layer arrives.
obo:FOODON_00003268 rdfs:subClassOf [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
    owl:someValuesFrom obo:FOODON_03411405 ] .
local:patch-660e709748e0 a local:Patch ;
    local:patchSection "mined" ;
    local:patchTarget obo:FOODON_00003268 ;
    local:patchProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
    local:patchValue obo:FOODON_03411405 ;
    local:patchRule "E: definition mining" ;
    local:patchEvidence "A tartiflette except that small squares of pasta, crozets de Savoie (usually made from buckwheat but sometimes durum) are used instead of potatoes." ;
    local:patchConfidence "medium" ;
    rdfs:comment "Extracted from FoodOn's own definition text and signed off per class. MEDIUM, not high, and the reason is in the definition: 'crozets de Savoie (usually made from buckwheat BUT SOMETIMES DURUM)'. That is a recipe choice, the same shape as the may_contain overrides that are deliberately kept out of the closure. Signed anyway under the recall-first policy, because the distinction that matters is which way an error falls: buckwheat allergy is anaphylactic and crozets are USUALLY buckwheat, so a buckwheat-avoider must see this dish. The cost is over-inclusion for the durum variant, which is the safe direction. TWO GAPS THIS DOES NOT CLOSE, recorded so nobody reads the dish as mapped: (1) croziflette is a multi-component dish (tartiflette base) and so also contains milk via reblochon, pork via bacon and allium via onion -- FoodOn asserts none of those and this bridge adds none of them; (2) the durum variant means it may contain gluten, and since buckwheat is gluten-free it will NOT appear on a gluten query. Revisit if a dish-level ingredient layer arrives." ;
    dcterms:creator "Matt" ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-10"^^xsd:date .

### malt syrup  --RO:0001000-->  barley plant
#   rule:       E: definition mining
#   evidence:   A syrup made from malted barley or grains.
#   confidence: high
#   reviewer:   Matt
#   Extracted from FoodOn's own definition text and signed off per class.
#   Definition: 'a syrup made from malted barley or grains'. The 'or grains'
#   hedge was checked and does not weaken this class, because FoodOn keeps the
#   generic reading in a SEPARATE class: `malted cereal syrup` (under
#   flavoring syrup) is the any-grain one, and `rice syrup` is its own class
#   under plant sweetener, so neither is touched by this edge. FoodOn also
#   already parents `malt extract` under `barley product flavoring`, which is
#   the ontology's own statement that unqualified malt means barley. Leaf
#   class, adds only itself. Barley malt syrup is a well-known hidden gluten
#   source, so the recall matters.
obo:FOODON_00005587 rdfs:subClassOf [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
